  "description": "Small and simple Json Parser to minimise memory allocation of Json.\n\t\tTheory:\n\t\t- String goes in\n\t\t- Get Memory of String\n\t\t- Translate memory area into key and value information not creating new regions or allocations unneccessarily such as additional string allocations\n\t\t- Pooled arrays are used for storing the key and value information, these are returned to the pool on disposal of the body.\n\n\t\tProvides access to classes JsonMemory and JsonSpan;\n\t\tJsonMemory is a parse on insertion, readonly struct based memory plotter allocating only the array space required and the string data that needs to exist.\n\t\tJsonSpan is a ref struct for Json access in methods, it is a parse on demand format using spans to read data, no array allocations only returning deeper JsonSpan bodies.\n\n\t\tEnumerators are included for Foreach looping however no support for IEnumerator.\n\t\tSupport of object in object path index. For example 'value[\"object.value\"]' is the equivalent of 'this[\"object\"][\"value\"]'.",
  "id": "NanoJson",
